interviewAnswer:'Calling an async function creates a coroutine object — nothing runs. Awaiting it executes inline within my current task. To get independent concurrent progress I wrap it with asyncio.create_task, which schedules a Task on the running loop; a Task is a Future-like object whose APIs it inherits except set_result/set_exception, because a Task computes its own result while a raw Future is resolved externally — that is why app code rarely touches raw Futures. I keep references to created tasks since the loop holds them weakly, prefer TaskGroup over gather for owned subwork because it cancels siblings on failure and raises ExceptionGroup, and never swallow CancelledError so timeouts and shutdown stay correct.',
