const glossaryRaw={
 'ACK':'Acknowledgement that a consumer successfully processed a delivered message.','ANN':'Approximate nearest-neighbor search: faster vector retrieval by accepting possible recall loss.','ASGI':'Python async server interface used by FastAPI/Starlette.','Backpressure':'Mechanism that slows/rejects producers when consumers/downstream capacity is saturated.','Batching':'Combining multiple items into one processing/inference operation to improve efficiency.','B-tree':'Balanced high-fanout ordered index structure used by relational databases.','BCNF':'Boyce-Codd Normal Form; a stricter relational normalization rule for functional dependencies.','Bloom filter':'Probabilistic membership structure with false positives but no false negatives in standard form.','Bottleneck':'The resource/stage currently limiting system throughput or latency.','Broker':'Messaging intermediary such as Kafka, RabbitMQ or MQTT broker.','Cache-aside':'Application reads cache, falls back to source of truth on miss, then populates cache.','Cache stampede':'Many requests simultaneously miss an expired hot key and overload the backend.','CAP':'Consistency/Availability trade-off specifically under a network Partition.','Celery':'Python distributed task execution framework commonly backed by Redis or RabbitMQ.','Circuit breaker':'Stops calls to a repeatedly failing dependency temporarily so it can recover.','Concurrency':'Multiple tasks making progress during overlapping time.','Consumer group':'Set of consumers coordinating ownership of Kafka partitions or Redis Stream entries.','Context window':'Maximum token context a model can process in one request.','Coroutine':'Suspendable Python async computation created by calling an async def function.','Cosine similarity':'Normalized dot product measuring angle/direction similarity between vectors.','CQRS':'Separating write-command and read-query models when different needs justify it.','Deadlock':'Two or more actors wait forever for resources held by each other.','DLQ':'Dead-letter queue holding repeatedly failed messages for inspection/reprocessing.','Embedding':'Dense vector representation learned so semantic similarity corresponds to geometric similarity.','ETag':'HTTP/object-storage identifier commonly used for cache validation or multipart upload part identity.','Event loop':'Scheduler that runs ready async tasks and resumes them when awaited I/O completes.','Eventual consistency':'Replicas may temporarily disagree but converge if updates stop.','FAISS':'Vector similarity-search library optimized for dense embeddings.','Fencing token':'Monotonic token preventing an expired distributed-lock owner from performing stale writes.','Focal loss':'Loss that downweights easy examples to focus learning on harder/rare examples.','Future':'Object representing a result that may become available later.','GIL':'CPython Global Interpreter Lock limiting simultaneous Python bytecode execution within a process.','GPU utilization':'Fraction of time GPU compute engines are active; high utilization alone does not prove optimal throughput.','Guardrail':'Control that detects/blocks unsafe or invalid AI behavior; should complement hard authorization boundaries.','HNSW':'Graph-based approximate nearest-neighbor index with strong recall/latency trade-offs.','Horizontal scaling':'Increase capacity by adding replicas/nodes rather than making one machine larger.','HPA':'Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler.','HyDE':'RAG technique that creates a hypothetical answer/document then retrieves using its embedding.','Idempotency':'Repeating an operation produces the same intended effect as doing it once.','Index-only scan':'Database query satisfied from index pages without visiting heap rows when visibility permits.','IoU':'Intersection over Union; overlap metric for bounding boxes.','Isolation level':'Database transaction rule controlling visibility/interference among concurrent transactions.','Jitter':'Random variation added to retry/TTL timing to avoid synchronized spikes.','Kafka offset':'Position of a record within a Kafka partition.','Keyset pagination':'Pagination using the last seen ordered key instead of OFFSET.','KV cache':'Transformer inference cache of prior key/value attention states for generated tokens.','Latency':'Time from start to completion; tail latency refers to p95/p99 slow requests.','Lease':'Time-limited ownership claim that must be renewed.','Little’s Law':'Average items in system = arrival rate × average time in system.','Load shedding':'Rejecting or degrading work intentionally to protect system stability.','LoRA':'Parameter-efficient fine-tuning using low-rank adapter matrices.','mAP':'Mean Average Precision; common object-detection metric across classes/IoU thresholds.','Materialized view':'Stored result of a query/aggregation refreshed periodically or explicitly.','MMR':'Maximal Marginal Relevance; retrieval method balancing relevance and diversity.','MQTT':'Lightweight topic-based pub/sub protocol common in realtime/IoT-style systems.','MVCC':'Multi-Version Concurrency Control; database readers use row versions/snapshots to reduce blocking.','N+1 query':'One initial query followed by one extra query per result, causing many DB round trips.','NMS':'Non-Maximum Suppression; removes duplicate overlapping detector boxes.','Normalization':'Relational schema design that reduces redundancy/update anomalies; also ML vector/data scaling depending context.','Object storage':'Key/object-based blob storage such as S3/MinIO for large immutable media/artifacts.','Observability':'Ability to infer internal system state from metrics, logs and traces.','Outbox pattern':'Atomically records DB change and an event row, then asynchronously publishes the event.','p95':'95th percentile; 95% of observations are at or below this value.','PagedAttention':'Paged KV-cache memory-management approach associated with vLLM serving efficiency.','Partition':'Kafka ordered log shard; also database table partition depending context.','PEFT':'Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning family including LoRA.','Pool exhaustion':'All reusable DB/HTTP connections are busy, so callers wait or fail.','Prefetch':'RabbitMQ limit on unacknowledged deliveries sent to a consumer.','Presigned URL':'Time-limited signed object-storage URL allowing direct upload/download without exposing credentials.','Primary key':'Column(s) uniquely identifying a relational row.','Prompt injection':'Untrusted content attempting to override model instructions or induce unsafe actions.','Quorum':'Minimum number of replicas needed to make a safe distributed decision.','RAG':'Retrieval-Augmented Generation; retrieve evidence and include it in model context.','Rate limit':'Policy limiting requests/resource use over time.','Read replica':'Database replica used for stale-tolerant read scaling and redundancy.','Redis Stream':'Append-only Redis log with consumer groups, pending entries and acknowledgements.','Redis ZSET':'Redis sorted set ordering unique members by numeric score.','Reranker':'Model/stage re-sorting retrieved candidates with a more precise relevance scorer.','Retry storm':'Synchronized retries amplify load on an already failing dependency.','Saga':'Multi-service workflow of local transactions plus compensating actions.','Semaphore':'Counter-based concurrency limit controlling how many tasks enter a resource at once.','Seq Scan':'PostgreSQL sequential table scan.','Shard':'Independent subset of a dataset routed by a shard key.','SLO':'Service Level Objective: target level for a reliability/latency metric.','SORT':'Simple Online and Realtime Tracking: Kalman prediction + association, typically IoU/Hungarian.','Structured concurrency':'Concurrency model where child task lifetime is scoped to parent operation.','Task':'Scheduled coroutine managed by the event loop.','Temporal voting':'Aggregate repeated predictions over time/track to produce a stable result.','Throughput':'Amount of work completed per unit time.','Triton':'NVIDIA inference server supporting multiple frameworks, batching and GPU model serving.','TTFT':'Time To First Token in language-model serving.','TTL':'Time To Live; expiration interval for cache/state keys.','Vector DB':'Storage/index layer optimized for vector similarity plus metadata retrieval.','Vertical scaling':'Increase capacity by giving one machine more CPU/RAM/GPU.','VLM':'Vision-Language Model that reasons over images/video and language.','vLLM':'High-throughput LLM serving engine; not the same as VLM.','VRAM':'GPU memory used for model weights, activations and caches.','Webhook':'HTTP callback used to push events to another system.','Write amplification':'One logical write causes multiple physical/index/replication writes.','YOLO':'Family of one-stage real-time object detectors.','Zero-copy':'Passing data between stages without unnecessary memory copies.'
};
Object.assign(glossaryRaw,{
 '1NF':'First Normal Form: each row/column intersection is atomic and repeating groups are removed.',
 '2NF':'Second Normal Form: 1NF plus no non-key attribute depends on only part of a composite candidate key.',
 '3NF':'Third Normal Form: 2NF plus non-key attributes do not depend transitively on other non-key attributes.',
 'BCNF':'Boyce–Codd Normal Form: for every non-trivial functional dependency X→Y, X is a superkey.',
 'CTE':'Common Table Expression introduced with WITH; names a query result for structure, reuse or recursion.',
 'Window function':'SQL computation over a window of related rows while preserving each input row.',
 'Container':'Running isolated process environment created from an image plus a writable layer.',
 'Container image':'Immutable layered filesystem/template used to create containers.',
 'cgroup':'Linux control group used to account for and constrain process resources such as CPU and memory.',
 'Namespace':'Linux isolation mechanism for resources such as processes, networking and mounts.',
 'Readiness probe':'Health signal saying an instance is ready to receive traffic.',
 'Liveness probe':'Health signal saying an instance is unhealthy enough to restart.'
});
D.glossary=Object.entries(glossaryRaw).map(([term,definition])=>({term,definition})).sort((a,b)=>a.term.localeCompare(b.term));

